---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
const trail = [{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy', href: '/privacy/' }];

/*
 * Every statement on this page must match what the site actually does. Before adding an
 * analytics tool, a newsletter, a contact form, comments or an embed, update this page
 * first and bump LAST_UPDATED in the same commit.
 */
const LAST_UPDATED = '14 November 2026';
---
<Page
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What Going Eagle collects when you visit, what it never collects, which outside services see your visit, and the choices you have."
  intro="The short version: there are no accounts, ads or analytics on Going Eagle, and the calculators never send what you type to us. A few things happen automatically whenever any website loads, and this page names each one."
  trail={trail}
>
  <div class="callout">
    <p class="callout-title">Last updated</p>
    <p>{LAST_UPDATED}. When this policy changes, this date changes with it.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Going Eagle is an independent golf instruction and equipment website. In this policy, "we"
    and "us" mean the people who run it. The site operator's details and a contact address will
    be listed on our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> once the site mailbox is set up.
  </p>

  <h2>What is collected, and by whom</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">What</th><th scope="col">Who receives it</th><th scope="col">Why</th><th scope="col">How long it is kept</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Anything you type into a calculator</th>
          <td>No one. It never leaves your browser.</td>
          <td>To work out your result</td>
          <td>Until you close the tab</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Standard request data: IP address, browser type, the page you asked for, the time, and the page that linked you here</th>
          <td>Our web host, Hostinger</td>
          <td>To deliver the page, keep the site secure and find faults</td>
          <td>In server logs, for the period the host keeps them</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Your IP address and browser details, when our typefaces load</th>
          <td>Google, through Google Fonts</td>
          <td>To send your browser the fonts the site uses</td>
          <td>Under <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Your light or dark display choice</th>
          <td>No one. It stays in your browser.</td>
          <td>So the site remembers it next time</td>
          <td>Until you clear your site data</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">A record that you clicked through from Going Eagle</th>
          <td>The retailer, if you follow an affiliate link</td>
          <td>So the retailer can credit us for a sale</td>
          <td>Under that retailer's privacy policy</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>That table is the whole list. We do not ask for your name, and there is nothing to sign up for.</p>

  <h2>The calculators</h2>
  <p>
    Every tool on this site, including the ball flight diagnostic and the handicap calculator,
    runs as JavaScript in your own browser. Scores, course ratings and answers you enter are
    never sent to us, never written to a database, and disappear when you close the tab.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
  <p>
    Going Eagle sets no tracking or advertising cookies. If you use the light/dark switch, your
    choice is saved in your browser's local storage. That is not a cookie, it is never sent to
    us, and clearing your site data removes it. A retailer may set its own cookie after you click
    an affiliate link, which the next section covers.
  </p>

  <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
  <p>
    Some product links on this site may be affiliate links. When you click one, the destination
    retailer may set a cookie so it can attribute a purchase to us. That cookie is set by the
    retailer, under its privacy policy, not ours. Affiliate programs report sales to us as products
    and commission due, not the identity of the buyer. Our
    <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> explains the arrangement.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
  <p>
    We do not run analytics, advertising networks or social media tracking pixels. If we add
    analytics, this page will name the provider and describe exactly what it collects before it
    is switched on.
  </p>

  <h2>Information you send us</h2>
  <p>
    There are no accounts, newsletters, comments or contact forms on Going Eagle today. If you
    email us once our address is published, we use your message only to reply and to act on any
    correction you send, and we delete it when it is no longer needed for that. If we add a form,
    comments or a newsletter, this page will be updated first, naming the service that handles them.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we are allowed to process this</h2>
  <p>
    For visitors in the UK and the European Economic Area: request data and font loading are
    processed on the basis of our legitimate interest in delivering a working, secure website.
    Saving your display choice is something you ask for when you press the switch. We do not
    rely on consent for anything, because we collect nothing optional.
  </p>

  <h2>Sharing and selling</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal information, and we do not share it for targeted advertising. The
    only outside services that see your visit are the ones named in the table above. We would
    disclose information beyond that only if the law required us to.
  </p>

  <h2>Where your data goes</h2>
  <p>
    Our host and Google may process the request data described above in countries other than
    yours, including the United States. Each describes the safeguards it uses in its own
    privacy policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>ask what personal information we hold about you, and get a copy</li>
    <li>ask us to correct or delete it</li>
    <li>object to or restrict how we use it</li>
    <li>opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information, which we do not do</li>
    <li>complain to your data protection authority, such as the Information Commissioner's Office in the UK</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Because we hold no accounts and no names, we usually have nothing that identifies you. If you
    have emailed us, we can find and delete that message. Requests go through our
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>, and we will not treat you differently for making one.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Going Eagle is written for adult golfers and is not directed at children under 13. We do not
    knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has sent us
    their details, contact us and we will delete them.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Every page is served over HTTPS, so what passes between your browser and the site is
    encrypted. Because we store so little, there is very little to protect, and that is deliberate.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    When we change what the site collects, we update this page before the change goes live and
    move the date at the top. We do not make changes that collect more about you without saying so here.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about any of this go through our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
